<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Shipcracker armor's jump, granted through VEF's CompAbilitiesApparel on
    SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker and fuelled by the CompApparelReloadable on the same
    def. Templated from VFEP's VFEP_PowerJump (1.6/Defs/AbilityDefs/Abilities.xml);
    the rules that differ live in ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump (planet:
    ranged, no sight test; space: unlimited range, sight required; landing-only
    breach blast) and the numbers in the BreachJumpExtension below.

    Tuning (2026-09-16, damage retuned 2026-09-17): fuelPerJump 20 of a 100-charge
    chemfuel tank (Aerial's numbers; 5 jumps per tank). breachDamage 20 (was 30):
    the pawn-facing number, split into 2 to 4 wounds by the SCWC_Breach def; Aerial's
    jump does 15, a frag grenade 50. Wall and building damage come from that def's
    factors (600 to a wall cell, 150 to a door or turret) and the shoulders'
    SCWC_BreachPower, which its worker applies to buildings only. breachArmorPenetration
    0.15 (Aerial's works out at 0.225, a grenade's 0.75): passed explicitly because
    GenExplosion otherwise derives penetration as damage x 0.015, which at 30 damage
    was 0.45 and negated marine armor outright. breachRadius 2 (down from 3 on
    09-16): a 13-cell footprint instead of 29, so a landing punches a door-sized hole
    through the wall it lands beside rather than levelling a room; vanilla's
    explosion still damages wall cells adjacent to the open cells it reaches. Wearer
    excluded; allies in the footprint are not, as with Aerial. requireLineOfSight is
    ignored by the ability class and set false only to document the planet rule.
    The blast radius is previewed at the hovered cell while targeting, and on a
    space map the reachable cells in view are outlined (see the ability class).

    Space flight (2026-09-17): a straight constant-speed run at spaceFlightSpeedFactor 3
    times the wearer's VFEP_FlightSpeed (36 cells/s at the base 12; Aerial's full set
    reaches 27 on a planet), capped at spaceFlightMaxSeconds 4 so a hop past 144 cells
    speeds up rather than drag. It uses Shock's Blast Off exhaust and fires
    SCWC_BreachJumpBlastOff at the launch cell; the flyer class explains all three.

    Text (2026-09-17): "breach jump" on a planet, "breach burn" in space (vacuumLabel
    on the extension, applied to the gizmo and tooltip title by the ability class).
    VFEP and vanilla otherwise swap a gizmo label only when the click does something
    else (grappling hook vs reload), and here only the reach rules change, but the
    space mode is a different enough experience (straight, fast, map-length, launch
    shockwave, its own icon) to advertise under its own name; "burn" is the
    spaceflight word for a straight engine firing, and keeping "breach" in both
    names ties them to the one fuel tank and landing. The description follows Power
    Jump's register and length (no numbers: VEF appends range, radius and cast time
    itself, and the range line drops out in space because SpaceRange is above its
    display cap; no fuel line: the tank takes astrofuel at half the charges under
    VGE1).
    The vacuum sentence lives on the extension (vacuumDescription) and the ability
    class appends it to the tooltip only when some loaded def can produce a space
    map, so players without Odyssey never read about a mode they cannot reach. A
    Defs-level patch from an Odyssey compat root was rejected: the tooltip is the
    description's only surface, and a patched description would drag its
    DefInjected entry into the gated root, where it would collide with the
    main-tree entry for the same field whenever the gate is open.

    Icons are placeholders borrowed from VFEP until the commissioned art lands:
    Aerial's Power Jump on a planet, Shock's Blast Off (spaceIconPath) in space.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>SCWC_BreachJump</defName>
    <label>breach jump</label>
    <description>Use the armor's drop thrusters to jump to a location, landing hard enough to breach walls and hull plating. The jump is short but needs no clear path.</description>
    <abilityClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.Ability_BreachJump</abilityClass>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/PowerJump</iconPath>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <keepCarryingThing>true</keepCarryingThing>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ShipcrackerWarcasket.BreachJumpExtension">
        <fuelPerJump>20</fuelPerJump>
        <breachDamage>20</breachDamage>
        <breachArmorPenetration>0.15</breachArmorPenetration>
        <breachRadius>2</breachRadius>
        <spaceFlightSpeedFactor>3</spaceFlightSpeedFactor>
        <spaceFlightMaxSeconds>4</spaceFlightMaxSeconds>
        <spaceIconPath>UI/Abilities/BlastOff</spaceIconPath>
        <vacuumDescription>In vacuum it has no range limit, but the way must be open.</vacuumDescription>
        <vacuumLabel>breach burn</vacuumLabel>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
